# The keel's signers (theseus-pw1q.1; two classes since issue 15): the keys whose signed commits may ack a keel guard
# finding (scripts/keel-guard.py) with a `Keel: <rule> <path>[, <path>…] — <why>` trailer. The guard reads this file
# at the range's base, never its head, so a branch cannot list its own key. Changing it is itself a keel finding.
#
# One key a line, `<class> <kind> <key>`:
#   routine  acks test-removed only (the owner, 2026-11-14): the key the agents who build this repository sign with.
#   owner    acks every rule. `owner none` holds the owner's place until his own key exists, and nothing can sign
#            his class meanwhile. Naming his key is one line: `owner gpg <fingerprint>` or `owner ssh <type> <key>`.
routine gpg 7CA7E3202D474BBA01DAF25477592FB1C703882E
owner none
